>> title: Cherry Clafoutis
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: cherry, custard, batter, oven, french
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.3: toss, then rest 15 min
>> step.5: whisk to a thin batter
>> step.6: bake at 375°F 40 min
>> step.7: dust, serve warm

Preheat the #oven{} to 375°F (190°C).

Butter a #9-in baking dish{} well.

Toss @sweet cherries{1%lb}(450 g, pitted), @kirsch{1%Tbs}(15 mL; or brandy) and let them sit ~{15%min} in the dish.

Whisk @eggs{3%large}(150 g), @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(65 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) until smooth.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(65 g), @whole milk{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL), @melted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) into @&(~1)eggs{} until it pours like cream.

Pour @&(~1)batter{} over @&(~3)cherries{} and bake at 375°F for ~{40%min}, until puffed and set.

Dust @&(~1)clafoutis{} with @powdered sugar{1%Tbs}(8 g) and serve warm.
